# First Night Is In Three Weeks | INT | Village Hall, Props Cupboard | NIGHT | gwen, dot | Name it | Looking for a decanter, they find a 1911 programme and a parish magazine's apology. {dot} says, mildly, that he was in on Tuesday | The Players learn who {thrale} is | 4 | props=programme+parish magazine+torch
# First Night Is In Three Weeks | INT | Village Hall, Stage | NIGHT | barnaby, ines, gwen, thrale | Find the rule | {barnaby} dies as if stung and the figure comes to the edge of the stage with its hand out. {ines} speaks her next line simply, to stop him shaking, and it steps back | {ines} sees what it wants | 5 | vfx=figure at stage edge+frost on footlights
# Get Good | EXT | Village Hall, Car Park | NIGHT | gwen, ines, barnaby | Choose the play | In the one safe place, by the bottle bank, {ines} lays it out: close, or get good. {barnaby} says he is good. Nobody answers him, which is the first honest silence he has heard | {gwen} chooses to go on | 4 | vehicles=parked cars
# Get Good | INT | Village Hall, Stage | NIGHT | gwen, ines, barnaby, dot, thrale | Rehearse under threat | A montage that is not one: one line, said again and again, the temperature the only note. {dot} confesses the wrong edition. {barnaby} says a sentence as if he meant it and looks astonished | | 6 | vfx=figure in wings+breath in cold air, props=prompt book
# Get Good | INT | Village Hall, Stage | NIGHT | barnaby, ines, gwen, dot, thrale | Lose the stage | The dress rehearsal. {barnaby} dries. The figure walks on, takes his mark and plays the part, perfectly, and will not go off. The exit sign cracks | {thrale} takes the play | 6 | vfx=figure performing+cracking sign+frost, stunts=glass breaking
# Opening Night | INT | Village Hall, Main Room | NIGHT | gwen, ines, dot, thrale | Open anyway | A full house in scarves, blaming the heating. {ines} carries the first half opposite a dead man who is better than she is, and holds | | 5 | crowd=90, vfx=figure performing
# Opening Night | INT | Village Hall, Stage | NIGHT | gwen, barnaby, thrale, dot, ines | Take it back | {gwen} goes on for a missing actor and is dreadful. The figure turns. {barnaby} hears her, properly, and answers. One true exchange in bad wigs. {dot}, from the corner: "House lights, Mr. Thrale." He nods, calls the curtain, and is gone | The Players take the play back | 7 | crowd=90, vfx=figure turning+figure fading, props=prompt book+torch
# Opening Night | INT | Village Hall, Kitchen | NIGHT | gwen, ines, barnaby, dot | Count the float | Urn, mince pies, takings of three hundred and six pounds. {barnaby} reads the parish magazine's verdict aloud from a phone: the second half dragged. They are delighted | | 3 | props=tea urn+float tin+phone
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; the first mixed-genre story, so there is nothing beside it to read it against yet
